1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,021
From your very first paycheck,

2
00:00:02,021 --> 00:00:05,794
modern culture hands you a remarkably narrow scoreboard:

3
00:00:05,794 --> 00:00:08,489
one single number inside a bank account.

4
00:00:08,489 --> 00:00:13,070
That single-metric obsession explains one of the strangest paradoxes

5
00:00:13,070 --> 00:00:14,283
of modern success,

6
00:00:14,283 --> 00:00:17,382
how someone can hit seven figures on paper yet

7
00:00:17,382 --> 00:00:18,594
wake up exhausted,

8
00:00:18,594 --> 00:00:19,201
isolated,

9
00:00:19,201 --> 00:00:21,761
and chained to a calendar they resent.

10
00:00:21,761 --> 00:00:24,927
As writer Sahil Bloom highlights in The 5 Types

11
00:00:24,927 --> 00:00:25,601
of Wealth,

12
00:00:25,601 --> 00:00:29,912
a genuinely rich life actually runs on five distinct currencies:

13
00:00:29,912 --> 00:00:30,721
Time Wealth,

14
00:00:30,721 --> 00:00:31,664
Social Wealth,

15
00:00:31,664 --> 00:00:32,607
Mental Wealth,

16
00:00:32,607 --> 00:00:33,685
Physical Wealth,

17
00:00:33,685 --> 00:00:35,100
and Financial Wealth.

18
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:37,999
Start with Time Wealth and Social Wealth.

19
00:00:37,999 --> 00:00:41,464
Time Wealth is not merely retiring at sixty-five;

20
00:00:41,464 --> 00:00:44,504
it is daily autonomy over what you work on,

21
00:00:44,504 --> 00:00:45,494
where you sit,

22
00:00:45,494 --> 00:00:47,545
and whom you build alongside.

23
00:00:47,545 --> 00:00:49,878
Writer Tim Urban ran the numbers:

24
00:00:49,878 --> 00:00:52,353
by the time a child turns eighteen,

25
00:00:52,353 --> 00:00:55,535
most of the in-person time a parent will ever

26
00:00:55,535 --> 00:00:58,151
spend with them has already happened.

27
00:00:58,151 --> 00:00:58,858
Meanwhile,

28
00:00:58,858 --> 00:01:01,615
the Harvard Study of Adult Development,

29
00:01:01,615 --> 00:01:02,959
running since 1938,

30
00:01:02,959 --> 00:01:07,272
found that how satisfied people were with their relationships

31
00:01:07,272 --> 00:01:11,019
at fifty predicted their health at eighty better than

32
00:01:11,019 --> 00:01:13,070
their cholesterol levels did.

33
00:01:13,070 --> 00:01:16,129
Next come Mental Wealth and Physical Wealth.

34
00:01:16,129 --> 00:01:18,423
Mental Wealth combines curiosity,

35
00:01:18,423 --> 00:01:18,979
purpose,

36
00:01:18,979 --> 00:01:20,091
and inner peace,

37
00:01:20,091 --> 00:01:22,942
the rare capacity to sit in a silent room

38
00:01:22,942 --> 00:01:26,835
for thirty minutes without drowning in status anxiety or

39
00:01:26,835 --> 00:01:28,920
reaching for a glowing screen.

40
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:31,284
Physical Wealth is daily vitality,

41
00:01:31,284 --> 00:01:32,535
restorative sleep,

42
00:01:32,535 --> 00:01:33,161
strength,

43
00:01:33,161 --> 00:01:35,108
and mobility across decades.

44
00:01:35,108 --> 00:01:38,584
Think of Physical and Mental Wealth as the leading

45
00:01:38,584 --> 00:01:42,268
digit 'one' standing in front of every financial zero

46
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:43,311
you accumulate.

47
00:01:43,311 --> 00:01:46,370
Stack six zeros behind a healthy one and you

48
00:01:46,370 --> 00:01:47,413
hold a million;

49
00:01:47,413 --> 00:01:50,680
erase that leading one and every zero behind it

50
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:52,140
collapses to nothing.

51
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:53,331
Here is where smart,

52
00:01:53,331 --> 00:01:55,297
hard-working people get ambushed.

53
00:01:55,297 --> 00:01:57,382
Between ages twenty-five and fifty,

54
00:01:57,382 --> 00:02:01,255
millions play what psychologists call the Deferred Life Strategy:

55
00:02:01,255 --> 00:02:03,042
aggressively liquidating Time,

56
00:02:03,042 --> 00:02:03,459
Social,

57
00:02:03,459 --> 00:02:03,876
Mental,

58
00:02:03,876 --> 00:02:06,855
and Physical wealth to stockpile Financial wealth,

59
00:02:06,855 --> 00:02:10,429
assuming they can simply repurchase the first four at sixty.

60
00:02:10,429 --> 00:02:11,263
Unfortunately,

61
00:02:11,263 --> 00:02:14,003
compound interest works in reverse on neglect.

62
00:02:14,003 --> 00:02:16,327
Neglected friendships quietly dissolve,

63
00:02:16,327 --> 00:02:18,590
missed childhood summers never replay,

64
00:02:18,590 --> 00:02:21,807
and twenty years of chronic stress and five-hour sleep

65
00:02:21,807 --> 00:02:25,620
nights carry biological interest rates money can rarely reverse.

66
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:29,026
Financial Wealth works best as a freedom engine,

67
00:02:29,026 --> 00:02:31,154
not an endless status contest.

68
00:02:31,154 --> 00:02:33,850
Kurt Vonnegut once told Joseph Heller,

69
00:02:33,850 --> 00:02:36,333
at a party thrown by a billionaire,

70
00:02:36,333 --> 00:02:39,171
that their host had made more money in a

71
00:02:39,171 --> 00:02:42,648
single day than Catch-22 had earned in its entire

72
00:02:42,648 --> 00:02:43,216
history.

73
00:02:43,216 --> 00:02:47,331
Heller replied that he had something the billionaire could

74
00:02:47,331 --> 00:02:48,111
never have:

75
00:02:48,111 --> 00:02:48,608
enough.

76
00:02:48,608 --> 00:02:51,375
Without a written definition of enough,

77
00:02:51,375 --> 00:02:55,490
every income jump simply pushes the goalpost further away.

78
00:02:55,490 --> 00:02:58,919
Put this framework into practice this Sunday with a

79
00:02:58,919 --> 00:03:01,071
ten-minute Life Portfolio Audit.

80
00:03:01,071 --> 00:03:01,475
First,

81
00:03:01,475 --> 00:03:03,021
score all five buckets,

82
00:03:03,021 --> 00:03:03,357
Time,

83
00:03:03,357 --> 00:03:03,828
Social,

84
00:03:03,828 --> 00:03:04,299
Mental,

85
00:03:04,299 --> 00:03:04,904
Physical,

86
00:03:04,904 --> 00:03:05,845
and Financial,

87
00:03:05,845 --> 00:03:07,527
honestly from one to ten.

88
00:03:07,527 --> 00:03:07,997
Second,

89
00:03:07,997 --> 00:03:10,889
write one strict Anti-Goal for each pillar:

90
00:03:10,889 --> 00:03:15,327
non-negotiable boundaries you refuse to cross during busy seasons,

91
00:03:15,327 --> 00:03:18,487
such as never missing three family dinners in a

92
00:03:18,487 --> 00:03:21,984
row or never trading a morning walk for low-priority

93
00:03:21,984 --> 00:03:22,387
email.

94
00:03:22,387 --> 00:03:22,925
Finally,

95
00:03:22,925 --> 00:03:27,162
put one concrete thirty-minute deposit on Monday's calendar for

96
00:03:27,162 --> 00:03:29,246
whichever pillar scored lowest,

97
00:03:29,246 --> 00:03:32,810
so your life rebalances long before crisis forces it.
